**Finding:** With predict_recoil (Z-exchange higgsino, sigma_n = 7.43e-39 cm^2, LZ 2.84 t-yr extended NR window, hard cutoff v_esc+v_E = 776 km/s), m_chi = 1100 GeV gives N_LZ = 1.97, 0.494, 0.085, 0.009, 0.00, 0.00 at delta = 350, 355, 360, 365, 370, 375 keV (peak E_R = 315, 320, 324, 329, 333, 338 keV). Log-linear interpolation gives delta(N=1) = 352.5 keV and delta(N=0.3) = 356.4 keV, so the window is only about 4 keV wide (N falls about 4-6x per 5 keV). The 248 keV event stops being accessible between 360 and 365 keV (v_min = 774 and 781 km/s). At m_chi = 1159 GeV (the tool's thermal mass), delta = 360 keV gives N = 0.135 against 0.085 at 1100 GeV. That moves delta(N=1) up by only about 1-2 keV, to about 354 keV.
