**Finding:** Abstract-level literature anchors from OpenAlex. (a) arXiv:2403.19598 (S. P. Martin, PRD 109, 095045, 2024) says a thermal higgsino-like DM "mass must be between about 100 GeV and 1150 GeV". (b) arXiv:2607.20588 (Bisal et al., 2026) says "NLO corrections lower the DM-nucleon cross section below the neutrino floor" for pure higgsinos, and that a pure higgsino "typically evades current direct detection limits". This abstract quotes no numerical cross section, so the target of about 1e-48 to 1e-49 cm^2 remains unsourced. (c) arXiv:2410.17137 (XLZD Design Book, EPJC 2025) reaches the neutrino fog, with 3 sigma evidence potential down to 3e-49 cm^2 at 40 GeV. (d) Planck 2018 papers 1807.06205 (overview) and 1907.12875 (likelihoods) were found, but the abstract of 1807.06209 (parameters) was not retrieved, so Omega_c h^2 = 0.120 +/- 0.001 is still unquoted.
